time alternately with the "s" key. Carriage return or space spring to mind 
(switch off rest-on-space of course). Trying this, it looks like repeat 
messages are suppressed, so you'll need to press 's' then <space> then 's' 
then <CR> etc. etc.. The inventory commands '*' '(' etc. seem to work each 
time. '"' is useful as you can only be wearing 0 or 1 amulets, meaning a 1 
line response in all conditions - just don't #name your amulet so that it 
wraps.

Or use the repeat feature and rely on it pausing if something interesting 
happens. You need to prefix the number with 'n' if using number pad for 
movement - e.g. 'n99s' - otherwise just type the number straight - '99s.'


